{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1229445-boon-economy-hows-it-work","id":1229445,"title":"Boon Economy. Hows it work?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-22T13:36:24-07:00","id":1229445,"title":"Boon Economy. Hows it work?","content":"how to do decide how great boon an action is<br /> <br /> is casting theban sorcery a greater boon then cruac, because willpower will be treasured more then Vitae.?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T07:31:46-07:00","id":1229800,"title":"","content":"Every exchange is unique. Having a Dragon that will cut your heart out so you can't die is not going to help if you need a new place to feed but if you know a Blood hunt is going to be called on you it's great, whether you can offer that service to another is also important.<br /> From the other side someone less powerful than you who you are protecting will cast rituals for far less than someone who does't need you ever if they're less able.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T08:20:56-07:00","id":1229801,"title":"","content":"I'd do the Dragon removing your heart on a <i>Trickster </i>of the Circle of the Crone, as a <i>Fool </i>doesnt deserve such consideration<br /> <br /> <br /> before going off on a suicide mission.<br /> <br /> A <i>Hero </i>would rarely be that likely to die.<br /> <br /> if your a Crone feeding entirely by blood price,or an invictus elder using Oath of abstinence.<br /> <br /> Or a Carthian radical<br /> <br /> Might work there too for a long period of time<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh on Pool of Forbidden Truth's? <br /> <br /> could it be used on another's behalf?<br /> <br /> SSafe to say a Acolyte would demand an EXORBIRANT fee for doing so, given the fact that it has a lingering penalty? <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh think a Kindred would be willing to do boon trading with Hunter's, Mages, Werewolves, Prometheans, or BEasts.<br /> <br /> Could see Ashwood Abbey doing so gleefully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 06-24-2018, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T06:08:40-07:00","id":1230255,"title":"","content":"If said Hunger, Mage, Werewolf, etc. understands trading favors and vampiric society well enough to barter for boons, then a vamp would likely do so. There are two considerations:<br /> <br /> 1. It's a bit like a pig trading favors; sure, but you're still food at the end of the day!<br /> <br /> 2. City/Covenant body politic may frown on the vamp's willingness to trade formal boons with creatures who should not know they exist.<br /> <br /> Formal boons are enforceable at the political level by at minimum (maximum is Princely edicts) ensuring failure to fulfill results in tarring of reputation. You don't have to go that far with creatures who are not part of political society, so long as the creature is willing to take your vamp's word in return for doing something. This is a basic human exchange.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T07:14:54-07:00","id":1230273,"title":"","content":"If you enjoy going invitations to Ashwood Abbey Parties, you may find yourself keeping your promises.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh Anything the Ordo can offer someone not a vampire, if it needs to offer a boon? <br /> <br /> dont see anything Coils can do for Mages or werewolves.<br /> <br /> but any Kindred could be deniable muscle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T07:18:50-07:00","id":1230274,"title":"","content":"I've played in a variety of settings from where &quot;favors to be named later&quot; was a joke to scam free errand runners to where favors had a set value based on itemized expenses required to fulfill it. Obliquely defined covenant positions like Sanctified Archivist, Dying Light Journeyman, Invictus Commissioner, and Carthian Lawyers actually had concrete roles in settings like that.<br /> <br /> As for other supernatural involvement, it depends on the setting. In most settings I played, no since they usually aren't enforcable. In 1st ed.where Invictus oaths were actually a thing and we used a suggested houserule in the Invictus book to allow blood potency to substitute for discipline rank prerequisites for oaths I did have a notary character who trafficked deals with mages who did and would occasionally be asked to &quot;upgrade &quot; contracts Acolytes made with spirits and loa. (I never did figure out IC how they knew to specifically request it and more importantly that she was capable of it and the ST never told me. But I always suspected IC that her sire had mentioned it was possible at some point to his ex lover. She did after all learn how to notarize oaths from him.)<br /> <br /> The closest thing in 2nd edition was a pledge that one of my characters has with a Winter Court fae noble where he and his do not interfere with or contact her and hers after he kidnapped her as part of an elaborate scheme of his to create hybrid children. He owes her the equivalent of a life boon after he broke it to request her help with something else and she agreed. Only to find herself sucked into another quagmire of pledges, oaths, blessings, glamours, and hexes to preserve kindred and fae secrecy. (No good deed goes unpunished.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 06-26-2018, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T07:20:55-07:00","id":1230275,"title":"","content":"Any idea if Pool of Forbidden Secrets Can be used on behalf of another? <br /> <br /> probaly only for MASSIVE boons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T07:56:48-07:00","id":1230283,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not. It's reminiscent of the Legend Lore spell from 2nd ed. AD&amp;D though. Where it's a good idea to research and use Identify and just about any other divination spells the lore ability etc. first to learn about something otherwise you just blew a lot of time and money to cast a spell that doesn't give you anything meaningful. <br /> But requesting a specific spell from a specific individual seems rather odd. Why is this Acolyte advertising she has it in her repertoire. Does she place so little worth on her Willpower that she'll sacrifice it to benefit someone else for the mere &quot;promise&quot; of a favor? And on the flip side of that, does the requester want &quot;her&quot; knowing about their particular interest and more specifically knowing everything they know about it already as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T08:09:07-07:00","id":1230285,"title":"","content":"Cruac cost Vitae NOT willpower.<br /> <br /> Though... the Requester MIGHT want to look into the Chorister Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T10:34:32-07:00","id":1230321,"title":"","content":"The condition afflicted when casting that ritual prevents willpower recovery until they resolve the condition which entails undergoing a detachment check. They're effectively giving up willpower expenditure until they play a game of Russian Roulette with their Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T13:39:04-07:00","id":1231438,"title":"","content":"Point<br /> <br /> Primordial Truths<br /> <br /> on that ritual?<br /> <br /> does a version of the ritual at 2 or 3 dots to allow another to look into the pool gain insights and the condition, seem reasonable?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T05:18:33-07:00","id":1231557,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't for game balance issues. That is effectively the other person casting the ritual and it's too powerful an ability for the xp cost. It also potentially allows the Cruac ritual to either pawn off the negative side effects consequence free or turn a ritual intended to be an information source into a powerful weapon against anyone they don't like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T07:07:35-07:00","id":1231574,"title":"","content":"it just seemed themanticly appropriate, like in the pool of lady Galadriel.<br /> <br /> So your saying if an invictus politico consulted them for such wisdom they'd point him to the Chorister Merit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}